  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, due to its excessive scale, design and poor siting, would not be in-keeping with the character and appearance of the host property and local area, would harm existing protected trees contributing to the important leafy, green character of the area, and would lead to less than substantial harm to the Riverside North Conservation Area. The harm to the Conservation Area is not outweighed by any public benefits, contrary to Paragraph 215 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policy D3 and HC1 of the London Plan 2021, Policy CS8, DM10 and DM12 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that the proposal would not result in an unacceptable adverse impact upon the longevity, health and appearance of the tree (which is protected via a Tree Preservation Order) adjacent to the southern boundary of the application site which contributes towards the character and appearance of the surrounding area, contrary to Policy D3 and G7 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8, DM10 and DM12 of the Council's adopted LDF Core Strategy April 2012. \r"
  ],
